  "notes": "{準備中|じゅんびちゅう} is a compound of {準備|じゅんび} (preparation) + {中|ちゅう} (in the middle of). Most commonly seen as a sign on shops and restaurants indicating they are not yet open.\n\nUSAGE:\nOften appears on the opposite side of a reversible sign from {営業中|えいぎょうちゅう} (open for business). Used both before opening hours and during temporary closures such as lunch breaks.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {準備中|じゅんびちゅう}の{札|ふだ}: 'Preparing' sign/placard\n- まだ{準備中|じゅんびちゅう}: still preparing\n- {準備中|じゅんびちゅう}の{店|みせ}: store that is preparing to open\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {営業中|えいぎょうちゅう}: now open for business\n- {開店|かいてん}: opening (of a store)\n- {閉店|へいてん}: closing/closed\n- {休憩中|きゅうけいちゅう}: on break",
